<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 2:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov- <BR> <BR>I for one appreciate your input and creative thinking, and have been amazed by some of the stuff you&#39;ve come up with being limited to googling from a hemisphere away from the crimes. <BR> <BR>From what I can see, Tom isn&#39;t picking on you, but is just protecting assumed-innocent people and his own and the website&#39;s well being &#40;by being careful not to make himself open to lawsuits for slander, etc.&#41;.  He&#39;s applying the same rules to others evenhandedly, and has actually been pretty patient with you. <BR> <BR>Skov: don&#39;t quote/paste more than a line or two from another website- instead post only the url or a link to the original text; also don&#39;t mention explicit names, addresses, telephone numbers, etc., of anyone who you might be categorizing as a &#34;suspect&#34;.  &#40;I suppose this probably excludes &#34;known&#34; police suspects, such as Bill Butterworth&#41;. <BR> <BR>Tom: am I reading between the lines correctly that linking to a site that might happen to mention these kinds of personal details about a theoretical &#34;suspect&#34; in a legitimate way &#40;for instance, a ham radio club website, or a phone directory&#41;, but not providing explicit, detailed, information to single out the reference at the linked site is okay to do on the catchbtk.com message board? <BR> <BR>I do hope, Skov, you can manage to see Tom&#39;s point and behave yourself so that we can continue to benefit from your efforts and passion for the case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
